  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Acting Now for Food Security and Resilient Food Systems - Sierra Leone</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this project in Sierra Leone we support smallholder farmers in the Port Loko, Kenema, and Bo districts to increase production of rice, cassava, and groundnut. The project supports them to improve access to better quality agricultural inputs (e.g. seeds), extension services and tools and strengthen their production capacity. In addition, the project aims to link farmer groups to traders, supermarkets and other buyers. The project also trains women and youth on nutrition, product quality requirements, intercropping approaches, post harvest losses and food diversification and goat husbandry. Men and boys are engaged at household and community level to address unequal power relations between women and men and champion women&apos;s economic empowerment.</narrative>
  </description>
